    "title": "Montana Tech volleyball earns thrilling reverse sweep - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Josh Margolis ,\n2 hours ago BUTTE, Mont. — Montana Tech volleyball started their final homestand of the season in dramatic fashion, pulling off a thrilling reverse sweep of No. 24 Dakota State (20-25, 23-25, 25-20, 25-23, 15-7). It was a well-balanced effort for the Orediggers, with three players recording double-digit kills. Payton Treadwell had 16, Kinnidi Willmore had 15, and Madison Biery had 10. Setter Rhys Layton had a double-double, with 29 assists and 11 digs. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
